Aerie-Purpose: Add the Aerie Guard section to Settings: a top-level route, its menu entry and its place in the page switcher.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (route.ts, router.ts, lazy_load.ts, BUILD.gn, settings_menu/settings_menu.html, settings_main/settings_main.html)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #103. The page, settings-aerie-guard-page, is a Lit element
(SettingsViewMixinLit(CrLitElement)) in the overlay, chrome/browser/resources/settings/
aerie_guard_page. The route /aerieGuard is a section of the basic page, like Search. The
page is imported by lazy_load.ts and wired the way patches/hardening/0003 wires the
Security hardening page (route, router type, lazy load, BUILD.gn). The menu entry follows
the Privacy entry, so the hunk in settings_menu.html sits next to the order Helium's
reorder-settings-menu.patch sets. The entry uses the settings20:shield icon that Chromium
already has; its text is the grd string aerieGuardPageTitle (patches/adblock/0022).

